            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 51,
              "start": 51
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Olson, Ohio offers an investment tax credit that reduces the franchise tax owed by in\u2011state manufacturers, while out\u2011of\u2011state manufacturers must pay the full tax."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4906558c4deb55aeede93c723ac2fb629c3e5ce686414d54f688ec7c95dcc40c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-4906558c4deb-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked whether any party other than the respondents might have standing to challenge the tax credit."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4906558c4deb55aeede93c723ac2fb629c3e5ce686414d54f688ec7c95dcc40c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-4906558c4deb-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia echoed the question, asking whether someone could be found to challenge the credit."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4906558c4deb55aeede93c723ac2fb629c3e5ce686414d54f688ec7c95dcc40c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-4906558c4deb-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 26,
              "start": 26
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Stevens, justice Stevens inquired whether the case would differ if the tax credit were replaced by a cash subsidy."
      }
    ],
